      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PAW PALMER (1) goes very well this trip starting 30 times for 10 wins and 12 minors. Hit the frame latest (22.47) when third at Geelong in a Grade 4. Looks suited here and rates on top. LOCHINVAR THOR (8) is a capable type and proved too classy last time to win by 0.9 lengths at Geelong in a handy 22.49 beating Where's Nassif. The form out of his last race has been franked. Deserves serious consideration again. ODDLY COOL (3) turned in a better effort at Sandown last start, finishing third behind Lektra Beta (30.05) in a Grade 4/5. Has the pace to be prominent. Comes out of a solid form race last start. Hard to beat again. WHITE NILE (2) can sneak into the finish with the right run.",
